  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A parallel plate capacitor with plate separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is charged up by a battery. It is found that on introducing a dielectric sheet of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mm</mi></math>, while keeping the battery connections intact, the capacitor draws <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> more charge from the battery than before. The dielectric constant of the sheet is ____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Without dielectric, capacitance will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Therefore, charge on it, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mi>V</mi></math></p><p>Now, with dielectric capacitance will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Hence, charge on it will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>V</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>d</mi></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
}